      "summaries": {
        "en": "Iroh is a modular networking stack in Rust that replaces IP addresses with content-addressed keys, solving connectivity issues in modern networks. It leverages QUIC, hole punching, and multipath for reliable peer-to-peer communication. You can use it to build decentralized apps, real-time systems, or resilient IoT networks without worrying about IP management.",
        "zh": "Iroh 是一个基于 Rust 的模块化网络栈，用内容寻址的密钥替代传统 IP 地址，解决了现代网络中连接不稳定、NAT 穿透困难等问题。其核心技术包括 QUIC 协议、打洞（hole punching）和多路径传输，实现了高效可靠的 P2P 通信。你可以用它构建去中心化应用、实时协作系统或物联网网络，无需手动管理 IP 地址，只需通过密钥即可建立安全连接。",
        "es": "Iroh is a modular networking stack in Rust that replaces IP addresses with content-addressed keys, solving connectivity issues in modern networks. It leverages QUIC, hole punching, and multipath for reliable peer-to-peer communication. You can use it to build decentralized apps, real-time systems, or resilient IoT networks without worrying about IP management.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "iroh stands out for does-anyone-read-these, holepunching, and memes in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Iroh is a modular networking stack in Rust that replaces IP addresses with content-addressed keys, solving connectivity issues in modern networks. It leverages QUIC, hole punching, and multipath for reliable peer-to-peer communication. You can use it to build decentralized apps, real-time systems, or resilient IoT networks without worrying about IP management.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
