      },
      "summaries": {
        "en": "DeepSeek-V4-GGUF is a quantized version of DeepSeek's Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model, making it accessible on consumer hardware. By converting the original weights into GGUF format with various quantization levels (2-bit to 4-bit), it dramatically reduces memory requirements while retaining most capabilities. This enables running a powerful MoE model on a single GPU or even CPU. Use it for local inference, fine-tuning experiments, or as a drop-in replacement in llama.cpp-compatible applications.",
        "zh": "DeepSeek-V4-GGUF 是 DeepSeek 混合专家（MoE）模型的量化版本，通过将原始权重转换为 GGUF 格式并支持 2-bit 到 4-bit 的多种量化级别（如 IQ2_XXS、Q2_K、Q4_K），大幅降低内存需求，使强大的 MoE 模型能在消费级硬件上运行。其核心优势在于保留大部分能力的同时，让单 GPU 甚至 CPU 都能运行。你可以直接用于本地推理、微调实验，或作为 llama.cpp 兼容应用的即插即用组件，探索 MoE 架构在资源受限场景下的潜力。",
        "es": "DeepSeek-V4-GGUF is a quantized version of DeepSeek's Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model, making it accessible on consumer hardware. By converting the original weights into GGUF format with various quantization levels (2-bit to 4-bit), it dramatically reduces memory requirements while retaining most capabilities. This enables running a powerful MoE model on a single GPU or even CPU. Use it for local inference, fine-tuning experiments, or as a drop-in replacement in llama.cpp-compatible applications.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "deepseek-v4-gguf stands out for gguf, quantized, and deepseek in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "DeepSeek-V4-GGUF is a quantized version of DeepSeek's Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model, making it accessible on consumer hardware. By converting the original weights into GGUF format with various quantization levels (2-bit to 4-bit), it dramatically reduces memory requirements while retaining most capabilities. This enables running a powerful MoE model on a single GPU or even CPU. Use it for local inference, fine-tuning experiments, or as a drop-in replacement in llama.cpp-compatible applications.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/antirez/deepseek-v4-gguf for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
